  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "releaseNotes": "fix(SQL): PSDO-2923 - handle the DBCC \"please reattempt\" transient without an unhandled throw. The DBCC-repair-failed branch in ExecuteSqlQueryNoReturn no longer throws (it was the only branch in the catch that did, so the transient escaped through TestValueInject.InjectStoredSettings as an unknown System.Exception plus a false-positive Trello card); it now returns the message string like every other transient/graceful branch. The repair-success path assigns the retried query's result to returnStr so a failed nested retry is not reported as false success. On an unresolved repair it reports a single AutomatedError keyed on database + server (so repeated statements against the same bad database collapse to one card via SqsClient's exact-message de-dupe), and skips that send when the DBCC CHECKDB call itself threw and ExecuteSqlQueryWithReturn already reported.",
